<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Halle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1694</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Martin Luther University of Halle-Wittenberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of Halle was founded in 1694 by Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-prussia">Frederick III of Brandenburg</a> in the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-thomasius">Christian Thomasius</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-hermann-francke">August Hermann Francke</a> and later Christian Wolff it became a leading centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietism">Pietism</a> and the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a>. It merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-wittenberg">University of Wittenberg</a> in 1817 and is now the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> University of Halle-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-halle.jpg" alt="University of Halle" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown ; svg from Lumu (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Double_seal_University_of_Halle-Wittenberg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
